      "text": "Two water taps together can fill a tank in $6\\text{ hours}$. The tap of larger diameter takes $9\\text{ hours}$ less than the smaller one to fill the tank separately. Find the time in which each tap can separately fill the tank.",
      "ideal_solution": "Let the smaller tap take $x\\text{ hours}$ to fill the tank.\r\nThe larger tap takes $(x - 9)\\text{ hours}$.\r\nTogether they fill the tank in $6\\text{ hours}$.\r\nIn $1\\text{ hour}$:\r\n$$\\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{x - 9} = \\frac{1}{6}$$\r\n$$\\frac{(x - 9) + x}{x(x - 9)} = \\frac{1}{6}$$\r\n$$\\frac{2x - 9}{x^2 - 9x} = \\frac{1}{6}$$\r\n$$6(2x - 9) = x^2 - 9x$$\r\n$$12x - 54 = x^2 - 9x$$\r\n$$x^2 - 21x + 54 = 0$$\r\nFactorising:\r\n$$x^2 - 18x - 3x + 54 = 0$$\r\n$$x(x - 18) - 3(x - 18) = 0$$\r\n$$(x - 18)(x - 3) = 0 \\implies x = 18 \\text{ or } x = 3$$\r\nIf $x = 3$, $x - 9 = -6\\text{ hours}$, which is physically impossible. Hence $x = 3$ is discarded.\r\n\u2022 Smaller tap takes **$18\\text{ hours}$**.\r\n\u2022 Larger tap takes $18 - 9 = \\mathbf{9\\text{ hours}}$.",
