      "ideal_solution": "Let the tap with smaller diameter take $x\\text{ hours}$ to fill the tank.\r\nThe tap with larger diameter takes $(x - 2)\\text{ hours}$.\r\nTogether, they take $1\\frac{7}{8} = \\frac{15}{8}\\text{ hours}$.\r\nIn $1\\text{ hour}$:\r\n$$\\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{x - 2} = \\frac{8}{15}$$\r\n$$\\frac{(x - 2) + x}{x(x - 2)} = \\frac{8}{15}$$\r\n$$\\frac{2x - 2}{x^2 - 2x} = \\frac{8}{15}$$\r\n$$15(2x - 2) = 8(x^2 - 2x)$$\r\n$$30x - 30 = 8x^2 - 16x$$\r\n$$8x^2 - 46x + 30 = 0$$\r\nDividing by 2:\r\n$$4x^2 - 23x + 15 = 0$$\r\n$$4x^2 - 20x - 3x + 15 = 0$$\r\n$$4x(x - 5) - 3(x - 5) = 0$$\r\n$$(4x - 3)(x - 5) = 0 \\implies x = 5 \\text{ or } x = \\frac{3}{4} = 0.75$$\r\nIf $x = 0.75\\text{ hours}$, then $x - 2 = -1.25\\text{ hours}$, which is impossible.\r\nTherefore, $x = 5$.\r\n\u2022 Smaller tap takes **$5\\text{ hours}$**.\r\n\u2022 Larger tap takes $5 - 2 = \\mathbf{3\\text{ hours}}$.",
