      "text": "A motorboat whose speed is $24\\text{ km/h}$ in still water takes $1\\text{ hour}$ more to go $32\\text{ km}$ upstream than to return downstream to the same spot. Find the speed of the stream.",
      "ideal_solution": "Let the speed of the stream be $x\\text{ km/h}$.\r\nSpeed upstream $= (24 - x)\\text{ km/h}$.\r\nSpeed downstream $= (24 + x)\\text{ km/h}$.\r\nDistance $= 32\\text{ km}$.\r\nGiven time difference is $1\\text{ hour}$:\r\n$$\\frac{32}{24 - x} - \\frac{32}{24 + x} = 1$$\r\n$$32 \\left[ \\frac{(24 + x) - (24 - x)}{(24 - x)(24 + x)} \\right] = 1$$\r\n$$32 \\left( \\frac{2x}{576 - x^2} \\right) = 1$$\r\n$$64x = 576 - x^2$$\r\n$$x^2 + 64x - 576 = 0$$\r\nFactorising:\r\n$$x^2 + 72x - 8x - 576 = 0$$\r\n$$x(x + 72) - 8(x + 72) = 0$$\r\n$$(x + 72)(x - 8) = 0 \\implies x = 8 \\text{ or } x = -72$$\r\nSince speed cannot be negative, $x = -72$ is discarded.\r\nTherefore, the speed of the stream is **$8\\text{ km/h}$**.",
