      "marks": 4,
      "text": "A solar power company installs photovoltaic panels in sequential rows. The first row contains $14$ panels, and each subsequent row contains $4$ more panels than the preceding row. The installation contains $25$ rows in total.\r\n(i) How many solar panels are installed in the 15th row? (1 Mark)\r\n(ii) What is the number of panels in the final 25th row? (1 Mark)\r\n(iii) Calculate the total number of solar panels installed across all 25 rows. (2 Marks)",
      "ideal_solution": "The installation forms an A.P.:\r\n\u2022 First term $a = 14$\r\n\u2022 Common difference $d = 4$\r\n\u2022 Total rows $n = 25$\r\n\r\n(i) Panels in the 15th row ($a_{15}$):\r\n$$a_{15} = a + 14d = 14 + 14(4) = 14 + 56 = 70\\text{ panels}.$$\r\n\r\n(ii) Panels in the 25th row ($a_{25}$):\r\n$$a_{25} = a + 24d = 14 + 24(4) = 14 + 96 = 110\\text{ panels}.$$\r\n\r\n(iii) Total solar panels across all 25 rows ($S_{25}$):\r\n$$S_n = \\frac{n}{2}(a + l)$$\r\n$$S_{25} = \\frac{25}{2}(14 + 110) = \\frac{25}{2} \\times 124 = 25 \\times 62 = 1550\\text{ panels}.$$",
