      "marks": 4,
      "text": "A student saves money every month to buy a laptop costing \u20b9$44,000$. She starts by saving \u20b9$1,000$ in the first month and increases her monthly savings by \u20b9$200$ each consecutive month.\r\n(i) Find the amount saved in the 12th month. (1 Mark)\r\n(ii) Find the total amount saved in the first 12 months (1 Year). (1 Mark)\r\n(iii) How many months will it take for her to save enough to buy the laptop? (2 Marks)",
      "ideal_solution": "This sequence forms an A.P. with first term $a = 1000$ and common difference $d = 200$.\r\n\r\n(i) Amount saved in the 12th month ($a_{12}$):\r\n$$a_{12} = a + 11d = 1000 + 11(200) = 1000 + 2200 = \u20b93,200.$$\r\n\r\n(ii) Total amount saved in the first 12 months ($S_{12}$):\r\n$$S_{12} = \\frac{12}{2}[2a + 11d] = 6[2(1000) + 2200] = 6[4200] = \u20b925,200.$$\r\n\r\n(iii) Number of months ($n$) to reach \u20b9$44,000$:\r\n$$S_n = \\frac{n}{2}[2(1000) + (n - 1)200] = 44000$$\r\n$$\\frac{n}{2}[2000 + 200n - 200] = 44000$$\r\n$$\\frac{n}{2}[200n + 1800] = 44000$$\r\n$$100n^2 + 900n = 44000$$\r\nDividing by 100:\r\n$$n^2 + 9n - 440 = 0$$\r\n$$(n + 24)(n - 16) = 0 \\implies n = 16 \\text{ or } n = -24$$\r\nDiscarding negative months $n = -24$, we get $n = 16\\text{ months}$.",
