      "text": "A manufacturer of TV sets produced $600$ sets in the third year and $700$ sets in the seventh year. Assuming that the production increases uniformly by a fixed number every year, find:\r\n(i) The production in the 1st year. (2 Marks)\r\n(ii) The production in the 10th year. (1 Mark)\r\n(iii) The total production in first 7 years. (2 Marks)",
      "ideal_solution": "Let the production in the 1st year be $a$ and the uniform yearly increase be $d$.\r\nProduction in 3rd year: $a_3 = a + 2d = 600 \\quad \\text{--- (1)}$\r\nProduction in 7th year: $a_7 = a + 6d = 700 \\quad \\text{--- (2)}$\r\n\r\nSubtracting (1) from (2):\r\n$$(a + 6d) - (a + 2d) = 700 - 600$$\r\n$$4d = 100 \\implies d = 25.$$\r\n\r\n(i) Production in the 1st year ($a$):\r\n$$a + 2(25) = 600 \\implies a = 600 - 50 = 550\\text{ sets}.$$\r\n\r\n(ii) Production in the 10th year ($a_{10}$):\r\n$$a_{10} = a + 9d = 550 + 9(25) = 550 + 225 = 775\\text{ sets}.$$\r\n\r\n(iii) Total production in the first 7 years ($S_7$):\r\n$$S_n = \\frac{n}{2}[2a + (n - 1)d]$$\r\n$$S_7 = \\frac{7}{2}[2(550) + 6(25)] = \\frac{7}{2}[1100 + 150] = \\frac{7}{2} \\times 1250 = 7 \\times 625 = 4375\\text{ sets}.$$",
