      "text": "If the mth term of an AP is 1/n and the nth term is 1/m, show that the sum of first mn terms is (1/2)(mn + 1).",
      "ideal_solution": "Let the first term be a and the common difference be d.\r\na_m = a + (m - 1)d = 1/n   --- (1)\r\na_n = a + (n - 1)d = 1/m   --- (2)\r\n\r\nSubtract (2) from (1):\r\n(m - n)d = 1/n - 1/m = (m - n) / mn\r\nSince m != n, d = 1 / mn.\r\n\r\nSubstitute d = 1 / mn into (1):\r\na + (m - 1)(1 / mn) = 1/n\r\na + 1/n - 1/mn = 1/n => a = 1 / mn.\r\n\r\nSum of first mn terms:\r\nS_mn = (mn / 2)[2a + (mn - 1)d]\r\nS_mn = (mn / 2)[2(1 / mn) + (mn - 1)(1 / mn)]\r\nS_mn = (mn / 2) * (1 / mn) * [2 + mn - 1]\r\nS_mn = (1/2)(mn + 1). (Hence Proved)",
