      "ideal_solution": "A number divisible by both $2$ and $5$ must be a multiple of $\\text{LCM}(2, 5) = 10$.\r\nThe numbers between $101$ and $999$ ending in $0$ are:\r\n$$110, 120, 130, \\dots, 990$$\r\nThis is an A.P. with $a = 110, d = 10,$ and $a_n = 990$.\r\n$$a_n = a + (n - 1)d$$\r\n$$990 = 110 + (n - 1)(10)$$\r\n$$880 = 10(n - 1) \\implies n - 1 = 88 \\implies n = 89.$$\r\nThere are **89** such numbers.",
