      "text": "In $\\Delta ABC$, $DE \\parallel BC$ intersecting $AB$ at $D$ and $AC$ at $E$ such that $AD = x$, $DB = x - 2$, $AE = x + 2$, and $EC = x - 1$. Find the value of $x$.",
      "ideal_solution": "In $\\Delta ABC$, since $DE \\parallel BC$, by Basic Proportionality Theorem (Thales Theorem):\r\n$$\\frac{AD}{DB} = \\frac{AE}{EC}$$\r\nSubstituting given algebraic values:\r\n$$\\frac{x}{x - 2} = \\frac{x + 2}{x - 1}$$\r\nCross-multiplying:\r\n$$x(x - 1) = (x - 2)(x + 2)$$\r\n$$x^2 - x = x^2 - 4$$\r\nSubtracting $x^2$ from both sides:\r\n$$-x = -4 \\implies x = 4.$$",
