      "text": "In figure, XY is parallel to BC of a triangle ABC and it divides the triangle into two parts of equal area. Find the ratio AX / AB.",
      "ideal_solution": "Given: XY || BC and Area(triangle AXY) = Area(trapezium XBCY).\r\nArea(triangle ABC) = Area(triangle AXY) + Area(trapezium XBCY) = 2 * Area(triangle AXY).\r\n=> Area(triangle AXY) / Area(triangle ABC) = 1 / 2.\r\n\r\nSince XY || BC:\r\nTriangle AXY ~ Triangle ABC (by AA similarity).\r\nRatio of areas of similar triangles is equal to square of ratio of corresponding sides:\r\nArea(triangle AXY) / Area(triangle ABC) = (AX / AB)^2\r\n1 / 2 = (AX / AB)^2\r\nAX / AB = 1 / sqrt(2) = sqrt(2) / 2.",
