      "text": "Find the ratio in which the point $P\\left(\\frac{3}{4}, \\frac{5}{12}\\right)$ divides the line segment joining the points $A\\left(\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{3}{2}\\right)$ and $B(2, -5)$.",
      "ideal_solution": "Let the point $P$ divide segment $AB$ in the ratio $k : 1$.\r\nUsing Section Formula on the $x$-coordinate:\r\n$$x = \\frac{k x_2 + 1 x_1}{k + 1}$$\r\n$$\\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{k(2) + 1\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}{k + 1}$$\r\n$$\\frac{3}{4}(k + 1) = 2k + \\frac{1}{2}$$\r\n$$3(k + 1) = 8k + 2$$\r\n$$3k + 3 = 8k + 2 \\implies 5k = 1 \\implies k = \\frac{1}{5}.$$\r\nThus, the required ratio is **$1 : 5$**.",
