      "marks": 3,
      "text": "A tree breaks due to a storm and the broken part bends so that the top of the tree touches the ground making an angle of 30 degrees with it. The distance between the foot of the tree to the point where the top touches the ground is 8 m. Find the height of the tree.",
      "ideal_solution": "Let the unbroken part of the tree be AB and the broken part bent to ground be AC.\r\nDistance from foot of tree to point C: BC = 8 m.\r\nAngle of elevation of top ACB = 30 degrees.\r\n\r\nIn right triangle ABC:\r\ntan(30) = AB / BC => 1/sqrt(3) = AB / 8 => AB = 8 / sqrt(3) m.\r\n\r\ncos(30) = BC / AC => sqrt(3)/2 = 8 / AC => AC = 16 / sqrt(3) m.\r\n\r\nTotal height of tree = AB + AC:\r\nHeight = 8/sqrt(3) + 16/sqrt(3) = 24 / sqrt(3) = 8*sqrt(3) m.\r\nHeight = 8 * 1.732 = 13.856 m \u2248 13.86 m.",
      "rubric": {
        "total_height": "1.5 Marks",
        "tangent_cos_steps": "1.5 Marks"
      },
