      "pyq_set": "Official SQP",
      "paper_region": "All India",
      "marks": 5,
      "text": "From the top of a 7 m high building, the angle of elevation of the top of a cable tower is 60 degrees and the angle of depression of its foot is 45 degrees. Determine the height of the tower (Take sqrt(3) = 1.732).",
      "ideal_solution": "Let AB be the building of height 7 m (AB = 7 m).\r\nLet CD be the cable tower of height H.\r\nDraw horizontal line AM perpendicular to CD such that DM = AB = 7 m.\r\nLet CM = h, so total height H = CM + DM = h + 7.\r\nLet horizontal distance BD = AM = x.\r\n\r\nIn right triangle ABD:\r\ntan(45) = AB / BD => 1 = 7 / x => x = 7 m.\r\nSo AM = 7 m.\r\n\r\nIn right triangle AMC:\r\ntan(60) = CM / AM => sqrt(3) = h / 7 => h = 7 * sqrt(3) m.\r\n\r\nTotal height of cable tower:\r\nH = h + 7 = 7*sqrt(3) + 7 = 7(sqrt(3) + 1)\r\nH = 7 * (1.732 + 1) = 7 * 2.732 = 19.124 m \u2248 19.12 m.",
      "rubric": {
        "tower_height": "1.5 Marks",
        "horizontal_dist": "1.5 Marks",
        "figure_and_tangents": "2 Marks"
      },
      "cognitive_type": null
