      "pyq_set": "Delhi Set 1",
      "paper_region": "Delhi",
      "marks": 5,
      "text": "As observed from the top of a 75 m high lighthouse from the sea-level, the angles of depression of two ships are 30 degrees and 45 degrees. If one ship is exactly behind the other on the same side of the lighthouse, find the distance between the two ships (Take sqrt(3) = 1.732).",
      "ideal_solution": "Let AB be the lighthouse of height h = 75 m.\r\nLet C and D be the two ships on the same side of the lighthouse such that the angle of depression of C is 45 degrees and of D is 30 degrees (angle ACB = 45 degrees, angle ADB = 30 degrees).\r\n\r\nIn right triangle ABC:\r\ntan(45) = AB / BC => 1 = 75 / BC => BC = 75 m.\r\n\r\nIn right triangle ABD:\r\ntan(30) = AB / BD => 1/sqrt(3) = 75 / BD => BD = 75 * sqrt(3) m.\r\n\r\nDistance between two ships CD:\r\nCD = BD - BC = 75*sqrt(3) - 75 = 75*(sqrt(3) - 1)\r\nCD = 75 * (1.732 - 1) = 75 * 0.732 = 54.9 m.\r\nThe distance between the two ships is 54.9 m.",
