      "marks": 3,
      "text": "Prove that the lengths of tangents drawn from an external point to a circle are equal.",
      "ideal_solution": "**Given:** Circle with centre $O$, external point $P$, and tangents $PA$ and $PB$.\r\n**To Prove:** $PA = PB$.\r\n**Construction:** Join $OA$, $OB$, and $OP$.\r\n\r\n**Proof:**\r\nBy Theorem 10.1, the radius through the contact point is perpendicular to the tangent:\r\n$$\\angle OAP = \\angle OBP = 90^\\circ$$\r\nIn right $\\Delta OAP$ and right $\\Delta OBP$:\r\n\u2022 $OP = OP$ (Common Hypotenuse)\r\n\u2022 $OA = OB$ (Radii of the same circle)\r\n\u2022 $\\angle OAP = \\angle OBP = 90^\\circ$\r\n\r\nBy RHS Congruence Criterion:\r\n$$\\Delta OAP \\cong \\Delta OBP$$\r\nHence, $PA = PB$ (CPCT). $\\blacksquare$",
