      "text": "A tangent $PQ$ at a point $P$ of a circle of radius $5\\text{ cm}$ meets a line through the centre $O$ at a point $Q$ so that $OQ = 12\\text{ cm}$. Find the length of $PQ$.",
      "ideal_solution": "By Theorem 10.1, the radius $OP$ is perpendicular to the tangent $PQ$ at the point of contact $P$:\r\n$$\\angle OPQ = 90^\\circ$$\r\nIn right-angled triangle $\\Delta OPQ$:\r\n$$OQ^2 = OP^2 + PQ^2$$\r\n$$12^2 = 5^2 + PQ^2$$\r\n$$144 = 25 + PQ^2$$\r\n$$PQ^2 = 144 - 25 = 119 \\implies PQ = \\sqrt{119}\\text{ cm}.$$",
