      "text": "A chord of a circle of radius $12\\text{ cm}$ subtends an angle of $120^\\circ$ at the centre. Find the area of the corresponding segment of the circle. (Take $\\pi = 3.14$ and $\\sqrt{3} = 1.73$)",
      "ideal_solution": "Given: Radius $r = 12\\text{ cm}$ and $\\theta = 120^\\circ$.\r\n\r\n1. Area of sector $OAPB$:\r\n$$\\text{Area}_{\\text{sector}} = \\frac{120^\\circ}{360^\\circ} \\times \\pi r^2 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 3.14 \\times 12^2 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 3.14 \\times 144 = 150.72\\text{ cm}^2.$$\r\n\r\n2. Area of $\\Delta OAB$ with central angle $120^\\circ$:\r\n$$\\text{Area}_{\\Delta OAB} = \\frac{1}{2} r^2 \\sin 120^\\circ$$\r\nSince $\\sin 120^\\circ = \\sin(180^\\circ - 60^\\circ) = \\sin 60^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$:\r\n$$\\text{Area}_{\\Delta OAB} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 144 \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} = 36\\sqrt{3} = 36 \\times 1.73 = 62.28\\text{ cm}^2.$$\r\n\r\n3. Area of minor segment:\r\n$$\\text{Area} = \\text{Area}_{\\text{sector}} - \\text{Area}_{\\Delta OAB} = 150.72 - 62.28 = 88.44\\text{ cm}^2.$$",
