      "paper_region": "All India",
      "marks": 5,
      "text": "Water in a canal, 6 m wide and 1.5 m deep, is flowing with a speed of 10 km/h. How much area will it irrigate in 30 minutes, if 8 cm of standing water is needed?",
      "ideal_solution": "Canal dimensions: Width b = 6 m, Depth d = 1.5 m.\r\nFlow speed v = 10 km/h = 10,000 m/h.\r\nTime = 30 minutes = 0.5 hours.\r\n\r\nLength of water column flowing in 30 minutes:\r\nL = speed * time = 10,000 * 0.5 = 5,000 m.\r\nVolume of water released in 30 minutes:\r\nV = L * b * d = 5,000 * 6 * 1.5 = 45,000 m^3.\r\n\r\nLet the irrigated area be A.\r\nHeight of standing water required h = 8 cm = 0.08 m.\r\nVolume of water in irrigated field:\r\nV = Area * height\r\n45,000 = A * 0.08\r\nA = 45,000 / 0.08 = 562,500 m^2 (or 56.25 hectares).\r\nThe area irrigated in 30 minutes is 562,500 m^2.",
      "rubric": {
        "volume_canal": "1.5 Marks",
        "water_column": "2 Marks",
        "irrigated_area": "1.5 Marks"
      },
      "cognitive_type": null
