      "marks": 3,
      "text": "The following table shows the marks obtained by $100$ students in a class:\r\n$$\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\r\n\\hline\r\n\\text{Marks} & 0-20 & 20-40 & 40-60 & 60-80 & 80-100 \\\\\r\n\\hline\r\n\\text{No. of Students} & 10 & 35 & 52 & 61 & 38 \\\\\r\n\\hline\r\n\\end{array}$$\r\nFind the mode of the data.",
      "ideal_solution": "The maximum frequency is $61$, corresponding to modal class **$60-80$**:\r\n\u2022 Lower limit $l = 60$\r\n\u2022 $f_1 = 61$\r\n\u2022 $f_0 = 52$\r\n\u2022 $f_2 = 38$\r\n\u2022 Class size $h = 20$\r\n\r\n$$\\text{Mode} = l + \\left(\\frac{f_1 - f_0}{2f_1 - f_0 - f_2}\\right) \\times h$$\r\n$$\\text{Mode} = 60 + \\left(\\frac{61 - 52}{2(61) - 52 - 38}\\right) \\times 20$$\r\n$$= 60 + \\left(\\frac{9}{122 - 90}\\right) \\times 20 = 60 + \\left(\\frac{9}{32}\\right) \\times 20 = 60 + \\frac{45}{8} = 60 + 5.625 = 65.63\\text{ marks}.$$",
