      "ideal_solution": "Construct Cumulative Frequency table:\r\n\u2022 Class $0-10$: $f = 6$, $cf = 6$\r\n\u2022 Class $10-20$: $f = 16$, $cf = 22$\r\n\u2022 Class $20-30$: $f = 30$, $cf = 52$\r\n\u2022 Class $30-40$: $f = 9$, $cf = 61$\r\n\u2022 Class $40-50$: $f = 4$, $cf = 65$\r\n\r\nTotal frequency $N = 65 \\implies \\frac{N}{2} = 32.5$.\r\nThe cumulative frequency just greater than $32.5$ is $52$, which corresponds to the class interval **$20-30$**.\r\nTherefore:\r\n\u2022 Lower limit $l = 20$\r\n\u2022 Cumulative frequency of preceding class $cf = 22$\r\n\u2022 Frequency of median class $f = 30$\r\n\u2022 Class size $h = 10$\r\n\r\n$$\\text{Median} = l + \\left( \\frac{\\frac{N}{2} - cf}{f} \\right) \\times h$$\r\n$$\\text{Median} = 20 + \\left( \\frac{32.5 - 22}{30} \\right) \\times 10$$\r\n$$= 20 + \\left( \\frac{10.5}{30} \\right) \\times 10 = 20 + 3.5 = 23.5.$$",
