      "text": "(a) What is the reactivity series of metals? Arrange Cu, Fe, Zn, and Mg in decreasing order of reactivity.\r\n(b) Describe an experiment with observations when zinc metal granules are added to aqueous copper sulphate solution.\r\n(c) State two conditions necessary for the rusting of iron.",
      "ideal_solution": "(a) Reactivity Series: A vertical arrangement of metals in decreasing order of their chemical reactivity.\r\nDecreasing order: Mg > Zn > Fe > Cu.\r\n(b) Zinc Granules in CuSO4:\r\nZn(s) + CuSO4(aq) -> ZnSO4(aq) + Cu(s).\r\nObservations: The dark blue copper sulphate solution becomes colourless, and reddish-brown copper deposits on the zinc granules.\r\n(c) Rusting Conditions: (i) Presence of oxygen (air), (ii) Presence of moisture (water vapor). Both must be present simultaneously.",
