      "text": "(a) Distinguish between minerals and ores. Name one ore of mercury and one ore of copper.\r\n(b) Explain the chemical extraction of mercury from its cinnabar ore with balanced equations.\r\n(c) How are metals located at the top of the reactivity series (such as Na and Al) extracted from their ores?",
      "ideal_solution": "(a) Distinction: Minerals are naturally occurring inorganic substances containing metals; Ores are minerals from which metals can be extracted profitably.\r\nMercury ore: Cinnabar (HgS); Copper ore: Copper glance (Cu2S) or Copper pyrites (CuFeS2).\r\n(b) Extraction of Mercury:\r\n1. Roasting: 2HgS(s) + 3O2(g) --(Heat)--> 2HgO(s) + 2SO2(g).\r\n2. Thermal Reduction: 2HgO(s) --(Heat)--> 2Hg(l) + O2(g).\r\n(c) Reactive Metals: High chemical affinity for oxygen prevents extraction via carbon reduction; they are extracted by electrolytic reduction of their molten chloride salts (e.g., molten NaCl at cathode: Na+ + e- -> Na).",
