      "ideal_solution": "(a) Sodium Reaction: Reacts vigorously and exothermically with cold water, generating sodium hydroxide and hydrogen gas which catches fire:\r\n2Na(s) + 2H2O(l) -> 2NaOH(aq) + H2(g) + Heat.\r\n(b) Calcium Floating: Calcium reacts less violently; the bubbles of hydrogen gas evolved stick to the metallic calcium surface, making it buoyant enough to float.\r\n(c) Chemical Differences:\r\n1. Oxides: Metal oxides are basic or amphoteric; non-metal oxides are acidic or neutral.\r\n2. Reaction with dilute acids: Metals displace hydrogen from dilute acids; non-metals do not.\r\n3. Electron exchange: Metals lose electrons to form cations (electropositive); non-metals gain electrons to form anions (electronegative).",
