      "ideal_solution": "(a) Heating a carboxylic acid with an alcohol in the presence of conc. H2SO4 catalyst produces a sweet-smelling ester:\r\nCH3COOH + C2H5OH --(Conc H2SO4)--> CH3COOC2H5 + H2O.\r\n(b) Saponification: Alkaline hydrolysis breaks the ester down into sodium ethanoate (soap) and ethanol:\r\nCH3COOC2H5 + NaOH -> CH3COONa + C2H5OH.\r\n(c) Carbon cannot gain 4 electrons to form C4- because 6 nuclear protons cannot stably hold 10 electrons; it cannot lose 4 electrons to form C4+ due to prohibitive ionization enthalpy. Therefore, carbon achieves an octet by sharing electrons.",
