      "marks": 5,
      "text": "(a) What is esterification? Write the balanced chemical equation for the reaction between ethanol and ethanoic acid in the presence of concentrated sulfuric acid.\r\n(b) What is saponification? Write the chemical equation for the reaction of an ester with sodium hydroxide.\r\n(c) What are micelles? Explain the cleansing action of soap in water.",
      "ideal_solution": "(a) Esterification: Reaction between a carboxylic acid and an alcohol in the presence of an acid catalyst to produce a fruity-smelling ester:\r\nCH3COOH + C2H5OH --(Conc H2SO4)--> CH3COOC2H5 + H2O.\r\n(b) Saponification: Alkaline hydrolysis of an ester into soap (carboxylate salt) and alcohol:\r\nCH3COOC2H5 + NaOH -> CH3COONa + C2H5OH.\r\n(c) Micelle Action:\r\nSoap molecules have an ionic hydrophilic head (water-soluble) and a long hydrocarbon hydrophobic tail (oil-soluble). In water, tails dissolve in the oil/dirt droplet while ionic heads face outward toward water, creating spherical micelles that lift dirt into suspension.",
