      "marks": 5,
      "text": "(a) Write the chemical name and formula of vinegar.\r\n(b) What is glacial acetic acid and why is it so named?\r\n(c) Write chemical equations for the reaction of ethanoic acid with: (i) Sodium hydroxide, (ii) Ethanol in the presence of concentrated sulphuric acid.",
      "ideal_solution": "(a) Vinegar: 5\u20138% aqueous solution of ethanoic acid (acetic acid), CH3COOH.\r\n(b) Glacial Acetic Acid: Pure anhydrous ethanoic acid. It freezes into ice-like crystals at 290 K (17 deg C) during winter, which gives it the name \"glacial\".\r\n(c) Equations:\r\n(i) CH3COOH + NaOH -> CH3COONa + H2O\r\n(ii) CH3COOH + C2H5OH --(Conc H2SO4)--> CH3COOC2H5 + H2O (Esterification).",
