      "text": "(a) What is an addition reaction? Under what conditions do hydrocarbons undergo addition reactions? Give an industrial example.\r\n(b) What is a substitution reaction? Write the equation for the reaction of methane with chlorine in sunlight.\r\n(c) State two properties that make carbon unique.",
      "ideal_solution": "(a) Addition Reaction: Unsaturated hydrocarbons add atoms or groups across double or triple bonds to form saturated compounds.\r\nConditions: High temperature in the presence of nickel (Ni) or palladium (Pd) catalysts.\r\nIndustrial Example: Hydrogenation of unsaturated vegetable oils to produce solid vegetable ghee:\r\nR2C=CR2 + H2 --(Ni catalyst)--> R2CH-CHR2.\r\n(b) Substitution Reaction: A reaction where an atom or group in a molecule is replaced by another atom or group without changing the remaining structure:\r\nCH4 + Cl2 --(Sunlight)--> CH3Cl + HCl.\r\n(c) Carbon Uniqueness:\r\n1. Catenation: The ability to form stable, long-chain covalent bonds with other carbon atoms.\r\n2. Tetravalency: Ability to bond with four other monovalent or multivalent atoms.",
