      "ideal_solution": "(a) Homologous Series: A series of structurally related organic compounds containing the same functional group, where adjacent members differ by a -CH2- unit (molecular mass difference of 14 u).\r\nCharacteristics: Same general formula, gradual gradation in physical properties.\r\n(b) Alkene Series (CnH2n):\r\n- 2nd Member: Propene (C3H6), Structure: CH3-CH=CH2\r\n- 3rd Member: Butene (C4H8), Structure: CH3-CH2-CH=CH2\r\n(c) Micelle Formation:\r\nSoap molecules (RCOO- Na+) have an amphiphilic structure: an ionic hydrophilic head (water-soluble) and a hydrocarbon hydrophobic tail (oil-soluble). In water, tails cluster inward dissolving the oil/grease droplet while ionic heads orient outward toward water, forming spherical micelles that lift dirt into emulsion.",
