      "ideal_solution": "(a) Esterification: Carboxylic acid reacts with an alcohol in the presence of an acid catalyst to produce a sweet-smelling ester:\r\nCH3COOH + C2H5OH --(Conc H2SO4)--> CH3COOC2H5 (Ethyl ethanoate) + H2O.\r\n(b) Sodium Bicarbonate Test:\r\n- Carboxylic acid reacts briskly with NaHCO3, releasing CO2 gas that turns lime water milky.\r\n- Alcohol exhibits no reaction.\r\n(c) Poor Conductivity: Carbon compounds form covalent bonds through electron sharing rather than electron transfer. They do not form free mobile ions or electrons in solution.",
