      "text": "Explain the process of double circulation in human beings. Why is it necessary to separate oxygenated and deoxygenated blood in mammals?",
      "ideal_solution": "1. Double Circulation: Blood flows through the heart twice during a complete circuit of the body:\r\n- Pulmonary circulation: Deoxygenated blood is pumped from right ventricle to lungs for oxygenation and returns to left atrium.\r\n- Systemic circulation: Oxygenated blood from left ventricle is pumped throughout body tissues and returns deoxygenated to right atrium.\r\n2. Separation Necessity: Mammals are warm-blooded (endothermic) and require high cellular energy to maintain constant internal body temperature; separation ensures high oxygen transfer efficiency.",
