      "text": "What is hydrotropism? Design an experiment to demonstrate hydrotropism in plant roots.",
      "ideal_solution": "1. Hydrotropism: Directional growth movement of plant roots toward a moisture gradient.\r\n2. Experiment: Place moist sawdust in a porous sieve suspended horizontally. Place germinating bean seeds in the sawdust.\r\nObservation: As radicles emerge from the bottom perforations, they curve back upward toward the moist sawdust rather than growing downward with gravity, demonstrating positive hydrotropism.",
