      "text": "State the two laws of reflection of light. Does light reflection obey these laws when reflecting from rough or irregular surfaces?",
      "ideal_solution": "1. Laws:\r\n(i) The incident ray, the reflected ray, and the normal to the reflecting surface at the point of incidence all lie in the same plane.\r\n(ii) The angle of incidence equals the angle of reflection (angle i = angle r).\r\n2. Irregular Reflection: Yes, the laws of reflection hold strictly at every single microscopic point on an irregular surface; diffuse scattering occurs because the microscopic normal varies across the rough surface.",
