      "ideal_solution": "Given: f = -20 cm, m = -2 (real, inverted).\r\nMagnification formula: m = -v / u -> -2 = -v / u -> v = 2u.\r\nMirror Formula: 1/f = 1/v + 1/u -> 1/(-20) = 1/(2u) + 1/u = (1 + 2)/(2u) = 3 / (2u).\r\n2u = 3 * (-20) = -60 -> u = -30 cm.\r\nThe object must be placed 30 cm in front of the concave mirror (between C and F).",
