      "text": "An electric kettle rated 1000 W operates on 220 V mains. Calculate: (a) the current drawn by the kettle, (b) the resistance of its heating element, (c) the energy consumed in 2 hours in kilowatt-hours (kWh).",
      "ideal_solution": "Given: P = 1000 W = 1 kW, V = 220 V, t = 2 h.\r\n(a) Current: I = P / V = 1000 / 220 = 4.545 A (approx 4.55 A).\r\n(b) Resistance: R = V^2 / P = (220)^2 / 1000 = 48400 / 1000 = 48.4 ohms.\r\n(c) Energy: E = P * t = 1 kW * 2 h = 2 kWh (2 commercial units).",
