      "text": "(a) What is an electric motor? State its principle and the function of split rings.\r\n(b) State Fleming's Left-Hand Rule.\r\n(c) What is the function of the earth wire in domestic electric appliances?",
      "ideal_solution": "(a) Electric Motor: A rotating device that converts electrical energy into mechanical energy.\r\nPrinciple: When a current-carrying coil is placed in a magnetic field, it experiences torque due to magnetic forces.\r\nSplit Rings: Act as a commutator to reverse current direction in the coil arms every half rotation, ensuring continuous unidirectional rotation.\r\n(b) Fleming's Left-Hand Rule: Thumb, forefinger, and central finger stretched mutually perpendicular: Forefinger = Field, Central = Current, Thumb = Force/Motion.\r\n(c) Earth Wire: Connected to a metal plate buried in the earth; provides a low-resistance path for leakage currents from metallic appliance casings, protecting users from fatal shocks.",
