      "text": "(a) Explain the underlying physical principle of a domestic electric generator.\r\n(b) What modification in design converts an AC generator into a DC generator?\r\n(c) What are the standard colour codes for Live, Neutral, and Earth insulation wires in domestic electrical circuits?",
      "ideal_solution": "(a) Principle: Electromagnetic Induction (Faraday Law). When a closed armature coil is rotated mechanically in a stationary magnetic field, changing magnetic flux induces an electric current in the coil.\r\n(b) Generator Modification: Replace continuous slip rings with a split-ring commutator. The commutator segments switch contact with the stationary carbon brushes every half turn, converting alternating output into unidirectional direct current (DC).\r\n(c) Colour Codes:\r\n- Live wire: Red (or Brown)\r\n- Neutral wire: Black (or Light Blue)\r\n- Earth wire: Green (or Green with Yellow stripes).",
