      "pyq_set": "All India Set 1",
      "paper_region": "All India",
      "marks": 5,
      "text": "What are Multinational Corporations (MNCs)? Explain three ways through which MNCs control production in other countries, and state one benefit to local companies.",
      "ideal_solution": "1. Definition: An enterprise that owns, controls, and manages production facilities in more than one sovereign nation.\r\n2. Three Ways of Controlling Production:\r\n- Direct Acquisitions: Purchasing domestic firms to immediately acquire established production lines and distribution networks (e.g., Cargill Foods acquiring Parakh Foods).\r\n- Joint Ventures: Partnering with domestic firms, supplying modern machinery and technology while utilizing local manufacturing facilities.\r\n- Subcontracting / Contract Manufacturing: Placing assembly orders with small domestic manufacturers for finished goods (footwear, garments, toys) sold under the MNC brand name.\r\n3. Benefit to Local Companies:\r\n- Influx of foreign capital to purchase advanced manufacturing equipment.\r\n- Technology transfer introducing modern management and production methods.",
