      "text": "Evaluate the role of Multinational Corporations (MNCs) in promoting globalization. State three positive contributions and two negative impacts of MNCs on developing host economies.",
      "ideal_solution": "1. Role in Globalization: MNCs act as primary drivers of cross-border trade, technology transfer, and capital investment, integrating national markets into global supply networks.\r\n2. Positive Contributions:\r\n- Capital Inflow: Deliver foreign direct investment (FDI) into capital-scarce industries.\r\n- Technology Upgrades: Introduce modern manufacturing equipment, managerial practices, and quality standards.\r\n- Global Sourcing: Open export markets for domestic suppliers and subcontractors.\r\n3. Negative Impacts:\r\n- Market Displacement: Well-funded MNCs can out-compete and shutter vulnerable small domestic producers (plastics, toys, batteries).\r\n- Labor Exploitation: Competitive tax and wage incentives may encourage flexible, precarious contract work without statutory protections.",
