      "marks": 5,
      "text": "What is meant by Foreign Direct Investment (FDI)? Explain three reasons why multinational corporations invest in India, and two policy conditions enforced by the government to protect domestic industry.",
      "ideal_solution": "1. Definition: Investment made by a foreign company to establish business operations, manufacturing plants, or acquire corporate assets in another country.\r\n2. Reasons for Investing in India:\r\n- Large Consumer Market: A rapidly growing middle class with rising purchasing power.\r\n- Low Factor Costs: Availability of skilled engineers and semi-skilled manufacturing labor at lower wage rates compared to developed economies.\r\n- Proximity to Regional Markets: Direct access to South Asian and Middle Eastern export corridors.\r\n3. Government Safeguards:\r\n- Sectoral Caps & Approval Routes: Reserving sensitive sectors (e.g., retail, defense) under mandatory government approval channels.\r\n- Local Sourcing Mandates: Requiring multinational manufacturers to source a percentage of components from domestic small-scale suppliers.",
