      "text": "Analyze five major human activities responsible for land degradation in India and suggest corresponding mitigation measures.",
      "ideal_solution": "1. Mining Activities: Mining leave deep scars and abandoned open-cast pits in Jharkhand, Chhattisgarh, and Odisha. Mitigation: Proper backfilling and reforestation.\n2. Overgrazing: Destroys vegetative cover in Gujarat, Rajasthan, and Madhya Pradesh, triggering wind erosion. Mitigation: Controlled rotational grazing and pasture management.\n3. Over-Irrigation: Perennial canal flooding in Punjab and Haryana causes soil waterlogging and soil salinization. Mitigation: Drip irrigation and regulated canal scheduling.\n4. Industrial Effluents: Untreated mineral processing dust and liquid industrial waste render arable soils barren. Mitigation: Mandatory wastewater treatment before discharge.\n5. Deforestation: Uncontrolled tree felling destabilizes topsoil. Mitigation: Planting shelter belts and stabilizing sand dunes with thorny bushes.",
