      "text": "Examine five major challenges currently faced by Indian farmers.",
      "ideal_solution": "1. Fragmented Landholdings: Generation-by-generation inheritance divisions create economically unviable micro-farms.\n2. Groundwater Depletion: Excessive tubewell pumping has lowered water tables in major farming states.\n3. Fertilizer Overuse: Excessive chemical fertilizer use has reduced natural micro-nutrients and degraded topsoil health.\n4. Input Cost Inflation: Rising prices of HYV seeds, pesticides, and diesel have lowered net farmer profit margins.\n5. Climate Vulnerability: Erratic monsoons, unseasonal hailstorms, and market price fluctuations create recurring rural debt cycles.",
