      "text": "Explain any five institutional and technological reforms introduced by the Government of India to modernize agriculture.",
      "ideal_solution": "1. Land Reforms: Post-independence abolition of the Zamindari system, consolidation of holdings, and land ceiling legislation.\n2. Green and White Revolutions: Introduction of High Yielding Variety (HYV) seeds, chemical fertilizers, irrigation networks, and the cooperative dairy movement (Operation Flood).\n3. Institutional Credit Facilities: Establishment of regional rural banks, NABARD, and cooperative societies offering low-interest farmer credit.\n4. Financial Security Schemes: Introduction of the Kisan Credit Card (KCC), Personal Accident Insurance Scheme (PAIS), and crop insurance against droughts, floods, and pests.\n5. Market Support & Media: Minimum Support Price (MSP) announcements and weather broadcasts via Krishi Darshan on radio and television.",
