      "paper_region": "Delhi",
      "marks": 5,
      "text": "Explain the institutional and administrative steps taken by the 73rd Constitutional Amendment Act of 1992 to decentralize democracy in India.",
      "ideal_solution": "1. Mandatory Periodic Elections: Mandated regular local panchayat elections every five years.\r\n2. Caste Reservations: Reserved seats and executive positions for Scheduled Castes (SC) and Scheduled Tribes (ST) proportional to population.\r\n3. Gender Quota: Reserved at least one-third (33%) of all elected positions for women.\r\n4. Independent State Election Commission: Created independent state election commissions to supervise panchayat and municipal polling.\r\n5. Revenue Sharing: Mandated state governments to share statutory revenues and governing powers with local bodies via State Finance Commissions.",
      "rubric": {
        "five_steps": "5 Marks (1 Mark each for distinct provision)"
      },
