      "ideal_solution": "1. Lack of Internal Democracy: Concentration of authority in top leaders without organizational elections or member consultation.\r\n2. Dynastic Succession: Leadership positions retained within dominant families rather than awarded on merit.\r\n3. Growing Influence of Money and Muscle Power: Wealthy corporate donors and candidates with criminal records dominate nominations.\r\n4. Absence of Meaningful Choice: Ideological convergence between major parties limits distinct policy alternatives for voters.\r\n5. Factional Defection & Opportunism: Shifting coalition loyalties prioritize personal gain over programmatic governance.",
